  "article": {
    "hero": {
      "title": "🔑 Property Management Name Generator",
      "tagline": "Names for a property management company, from Well Kept Property Management to Gable Lettings."
    },
    "intro": "Good property management names sound steady and reachable: a surname or a place with \"Property Management\", or a word about keys and good order like <em>In Good Order</em>. Name your business with this **Property Management Name Generator**: for rental and lettings managers, block and HOA managers, holiday-let hosts and commercial property managers. Pick a style and what you manage, or add your first name or town.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Eight good property management names",
        "content": "<p>All eight came from the generator:</p><ul><li><strong>In Good Order Property Management</strong>: tells landlords their buildings will be looked after.</li><li><strong>Property Sorted</strong>: short and reassuring for busy landlords.</li><li><strong>Good Bones Managed Property</strong>: a builder's phrase for a sound house.</li><li><strong>Cartwright Property Managers</strong>: a surname, which sounds established.</li><li><strong>Kendall &amp; Mather</strong>: a classic two-name firm.</li><li><strong>Quoin Property Managers</strong>: a quoin is a cornerstone, an apt word for a building firm.</li><li><strong>Dovecote Property Management</strong>: a gentle, memorable modern name.</li><li><strong>Hampton Property Office</strong>: a local name, for a firm with a high-street office.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "How property managers are named",
        "content": "<p>Landlords, residents and leaseholders want someone dependable who answers the phone, so names lean on surnames, places, building words (lintel, quoin, gable) and phrases about upkeep. If you specialise, say so: \"Lettings\" for UK rentals, \"Block Management\" for flats, \"HOA Management\" in the US, \"Stays\" for holiday lets.</p><p><strong>Rules to know:</strong> in the UK, letting agents and property managers must belong to a government-approved redress scheme, and in England they must also belong to a client money protection (CMP) scheme if they hold client money. \"Chartered Surveyors\" and \"RICS\" are for RICS-regulated firms only. In the US, \"Realtor\" is a trade mark of the National Association of Realtors, and many states require a real estate broker's licence to manage rentals for others.</p>"
      },
      {
        "heading": "Check it's free before you print the sign",
        "content": "<p>Every name here has a Check button. Press it before you order business cards, and run through these yourself:</p><ul><li><strong>The company register:</strong> Companies House in the UK, or your state's business register in the US.</li><li><strong>Trade marks:</strong> search the UK IPO or USPTO for the same or a similar name in your field.</li><li><strong>Domains and handles:</strong> a matching .co.uk or .com, and the same handle on the platforms your clients use.</li><li><strong>Booking sites:</strong> keep clear of names like Airbnb in your business name, even if you list there.</li></ul><p>The <a href=\"../business-name-checker.html\">Business Name Checker</a> runs the first checks for you, and <a href=\"../guides/business-naming-best-practices.html\">Business Naming Best Practices</a> explains them in more detail. This is general guidance, not legal advice.</p><p>For sales as well as lettings, try the <a href=\"real-estate-name-generator.html\">Real Estate Name Generator</a>, and for the cleaners you'll book between tenants, the <a href=\"cleaning-business-name-generator.html\">Cleaning Business Name Generator</a>.</p><p>For more, see all the <a href=\"../categories/biz_services-names.html\">professional and creative business name generators</a>.</p>"
      }
    ],
    "faqs": [
      {
        "question": "What are good property management company names?",
        "answer": "Steady, local-sounding names: a surname (Cartwright Property Managers), a place (Hampton Property Office), or a phrase about good upkeep (In Good Order Property Management). Say what you manage if you specialise."
      },
      {
        "question": "What makes a good property management company name?",
        "answer": "Landlords and residents want someone steady and reachable, so surnames, place names and words about keys, upkeep and good order work well (\"Well Kept Property Management\", \"Hartley Estate Management\"). Say what you manage if you specialise: \"Block Management\" for UK flats, \"HOA Management\" in the US, \"Stays\" or \"Holiday Lets\" for short lets. Keep clear of big agents' and booking sites' names."
      },
      {
        "question": "Are there any words a property manager can't use?",
        "answer": "Avoid \"Chartered Surveyors\" and \"RICS\" unless you are RICS-regulated, and \"Realtor\", a trade mark of the US National Association of Realtors. Keep booking sites' names, such as Airbnb, out of your name. In the UK, letting and property management agents must join a government-approved redress scheme, and in England a client money protection scheme too. In many US states, managing rentals for others needs a real estate broker's licence."
      },
      {
        "question": "How do I check a property management name is free?",
        "answer": "Press Check on any name to see whether it's free as a company, a domain and a social media handle. In the UK, search Companies House; in the US, search your state's business register and the USPTO trade mark search. Check your local area too, as two similar names nearby confuse customers."
      }
    ]
  },
